---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteMeta } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${siteMeta.name}.`}>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="identity">{siteMeta.identity}</p>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I am Phillip Trummer, an AI systems researcher and product engineer based in Zurich. I work
        where long-running agent infrastructure, GPU performance engineering, and production
        software meet.
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <p>
      At Schranner Negotiation Institute, I lead product development for the
      <a href="https://platform.schranner.com">AI-driven negotiation training platform</a>,
      combining roadmap ownership and team leadership with hands-on system architecture. The
      product spans a full-stack web application, Python services, real-time voice agents,
      automated feedback, and cloud delivery.
    </p>
    <p>
      Previously, as Vice-President and Project Leader at ETH juniors, I led consulting and
      recruitment mandates for clients including Roche, Zürcher Kantonalbank, IKEA, and Axpo. The
      work spanned AI systems, data products, market strategy, and organizational growth.
    </p>
    <p>
      As a Student Partner at Founderful Campus, I scouted and supported student founders across
      ETH Zurich, connecting promising teams with Founderful's venture network and initial funding.
    </p>

    <h2 id="research">Research</h2>
    <p>
      My master's thesis, VibeKernel, uses GPU kernel optimization as an objective systems
      environment for studying long-running agents. Kernels must be retuned as hardware
      generations and workloads change, while expert optimization remains concentrated on
      mainstream operations and flagship architectures.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am investigating how harness design, including structured memory, experiment versioning,
      and session-handling policies, can make that optimization process more autonomous,
      persistent, and broadly applicable. Recent work also includes agent/database co-design and
      GPU-backed systems.
    </p>

    <h2>Now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Working on an ETH MSc in Electrical Engineering and Information Technology.</li>
      <li>Developing VibeKernel and its reproducible CUDA evaluation environment.</li>
      <li>Leading an AI product from roadmap and architecture through production delivery.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
